SOURCE
https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/2479

STEPS TAKEN
Section 1: Public Warning Siren
The alerts fired on the 5th of February. Oof, they were rated high as well. What was the name of the alert?
SecurityAlerts
| where severity == "high"
| where timestamp >= datetime(2026-02-05)
Answer: Trojan.IoTBot.PhantomGrid

What is the filepath mentioned in the alert?
Answer: /tmp/iot-update.bin

On how many devices does the file appear?
FileCreationEvents
| where filename == "iot-update.bin"
Answer: 28

When did it first appear? (Paste the timestamp in the TZ format, ISO8601 in the ADX settings.)
Answer: 2026-02-05T03:33:12.000Z

Which VLAN contains the most devices?
DeviceInfo
| summarize count() by vlan
Answer: room_iot


Section 2: Heartbeat Monitor
What is the name of the process involved in the execution of the commands you found?
ProcessEvents
| where timestamp >= datetime(2026-02-05)
Answer: sh

What interval was provided for the beaconing?
Answer: 60

What is the domain hardcoded in the commands?
Answer: iot-botnet-c2.net

Which IP address did the domain resolve to?
PassiveDns
| where domain == "iot-botnet-c2.net"
| where qtype == "A"
Answer: 185.203.116.45

How many times did a connection happen to the threat actor's IP?
NetworkFlow
| where dest_ip == "185.203.116.45"
Answer: 113037

How many days did the beaconing last?
NetworkFlow
| where dest_ip == '185.203.116.45'
| make-series beacon = count() on timestamp from datetime(2026-02-05T03:35:52.000Z) to datetime(2026-02-11T23:59:58.000Z) step 1h by src_ip
| render timechart
Answer: 6


Section 3: Screaming Into The Void
What type of attack is often performed using a botnet?
Answer: DDOS

What is the IP address with the highest number of hits?
NetworkFlow
| where timestamp >= datetime(2026-02-11)
| summarize count() by dest_ip
Answer: 45.95.147.236

How many times total was that IP hit?
NetworkFlow
| where dest_ip == "45.95.147.236"
Answer: 18925

When was the first connection made? (same as before, TZ format)
Answer: 2026-02-10T04:42:21.000Z

How many 'bursts' were there?
NetworkFlow
| where dest_ip == "45.95.147.236"
| distinct timestamp
Answer: 757

What is the full command that launched the attack?
Answer: /tmp/iot-update.bin --attack=udp --target=45.95.147.236 --port=80


Section 4: Knock-Knock
Which other domain in .net is linked to that IP?
PassiveDns
| where rdata == "185.203.116.45"
| distinct domain
Answer: hotel-firmware-check.net

Let's pivot on those domains to find all the associated IP addresses. Which IP address is the longest?
let dmns=
PassiveDns
| where rdata == "185.203.116.45"
| distinct domain;
PassiveDns
| where domain in (dmns)
| where qtype == "A"
| distinct rdata
Answer: 116.184.156.238

Which IP address repeatedly tried connecting to the IoT devices?
let dmns=
PassiveDns
| where rdata == "185.203.116.45"
| distinct domain;
let ips=
PassiveDns
| where domain in (dmns)
| where qtype == "A"
| distinct rdata;
NetworkFlow
| where src_ip in (ips)
Answer: 7.22.171.109

How many ports were repeatedly scanned?
let dmns=
PassiveDns
| where rdata == "185.203.116.45"
| distinct domain;
let ips=
PassiveDns
| where domain in (dmns)
| where qtype == "A"
| distinct rdata;
NetworkFlow
| where src_ip in (ips)
| summarize count() by dest_port
Answer: 9

Two of those ports are typical for IoT devices, one more secure than the other. Which protocol do they use?
Answer: MQTT

What are the first two words of the description for each and every login attempts?
let dmns=
PassiveDns
| where rdata == "185.203.116.45"
| distinct domain;
let ips=
PassiveDns
| where domain in (dmns)
| where qtype == "A"
| distinct rdata;
AuthenticationEvents
| where src_ip in (ips)
Answer: Default credential
